Package: AKCatchments
Type: Package
Title: Delineate and Characterize Alaska Stream Catchments with Documented Uncertainty
Version: 0.2.0.9000
Authors@R: person("Caleb", "Robbins", email = "robbinscalebj@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Delineates the catchment draining to a stream point anywhere in Alaska
    from the best available elevation data (by default the statewide 5 m IfSAR
    bare-earth terrain model), checks each delineation for the failure modes that
    automated D8 routing is prone to, compares it with reference flowlines,
    hand-drawn catchments and USGS StreamStats, and always draws it on satellite
    imagery so it can be checked by eye. Summarises topography, climate, snow,
    land cover, permafrost, geology, soils, fire history and alder cover for each
    catchment, carrying the uncertainty of every value in companion columns,
    with a catalog of layers and alternates and a provenance record for every
    value added. Observations (stream temperature, USGS daily values, your own
    chemistry) share one schema and are linked to the catchments.
